review_comments.body:
@squah-confluent 
An earlier revision made a defensive copy here. I removed it after the discussion about whether it was necessary, reasoning that the coordinator only reads the output and reconstructs immutable assignments during replay.

I hadn't fully considered assignor offloading. Since record building can be delayed until after another group invokes the assignor, I agree that we should restore the defensive copy here even if cost is quite expensive. 

@dajac 
What do you think?

